SmartCare v0.4 – Domain Implementation Workbook
1. UML‑to‑Code Trace:
| UML Element        | Python Element            | Implemented? | Notes                                      |
|--------------------|---------------------------|--------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Patient class      | Patient class             | Yes          | Attributes match UML (id, name, contact)   |
| Practitioner class | Practitioner class        | Yes          | Availability + schedule implemented        |
| Appointment class  | Appointment class         | Yes          | Links patient + practitioner               |
| Associations       | Object references         | Yes          | Appointment stores patient & practitioner  |
| Multiplicities     | Lists (history/schedule)  | Yes          | Patient.history & Practitioner.schedule    |
| Status invariant   | Private status + methods  | Yes          | Only legal transitions allowed             |

2. Domain Invariants:
| Class        | Invariant / Rule                                      | How Protected                                      |
|--------------|--------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| Patient      | patientID cannot change                               | No setter; assigned once in __init__               |
| Practitioner | availability must follow clinic rules                  | Updated only through controlled method             |
| Appointment  | status must follow legal transitions (e.g., S→C)      | Private status; changed only via cancel()/complete()|
| Appointment  | must always link valid patient + practitioner          | Constructor requires both objects                  |
| Appointment  | time/date cannot be changed after creation             | No public setter for date/time                     |

3. Composition / Inheritance Decisions:
| Relationship              | Decision               | Rationale                                           |
|---------------------------|------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| Appointment ↔ Patient     | Composition/association| Appointment *has a* patient; not a subtype         |
| Appointment ↔ Practitioner| Composition/association| Appointment *has a* practitioner                    |
| Doctor ↔ Practitioner     | Inheritance            | Doctor *is a* type of practitioner                 |
| Clinic ↔ Appointment      | Composition/association| Clinic *contains* appointments; aggregate root     |

4. AI Pair‑Programming Record:
| AI Contribution                     | Conforms? | Decision   | Reason                                           | Verification                     |
|-------------------------------------|-----------|------------|--------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| Add NotificationManager             | No        | Rejected   | Out of scope; no requirement supports it         | Requirements FR/NFR checked      |
| Add AppointmentManager              | No        | Rejected   | Implementation detail, not domain concept        | UML + domain rules checked       |
| Add UserRole class                  | Yes       | Accepted   | Supported by NFR-03 (security)                   | Requirement ID verified          |
| Add ScheduleView class              | Partial   | Modified   | Behaviour exists but not a standalone class      | FR-09 supports behaviour only    |
| Add inheritance from PatientRecord  | No        | Rejected   | Incorrect hierarchy; Appointment ≠ PatientRecord | Domain model checked             |

5. Updated UML:
Justified Change: Added UserRole class
Reason: During implementation, access control became necessary to protect patient/practitioner data (supported by NFR‑03).
This is a legitimate domain concept, not an invented feature.

